menu "Micro OS filesystems"

    config MICRO_OS_FS_FAT32
        bool "FAT12/16/32, read and write"
        default n
        help
            Read and write the volume of a card or a disk that another
            system made. The filesystem has no modes, no owners and no
            time of its own: stat answers zero for the first two, and
            chmod and chown are not supported. There is no journal, so a
            power cut in the middle of a change is a volume a checker has
            to look at.

endmenu
